{"text": "\u2018Timothy C. Capone\n\nProfessional Summary\n\nInstituted expectations that led to increased student achievement in diverse communities\nLed two schools to Bronze Award (awarded by US News & World Report)\nLed a Priority School (1 of the 4 lowest performing schools) out of Schoo! Improvement\nculminating with a Superior ranking designated by the state Department of Education\nEstablished the International Baccalaureate Program at Sussex Central High School\nIncreased Advanced Placement participants and passing scores\nIncreased student achievement by 20% on state assessments 5 times\nDistrict's student growth outperformed 72% and 83% respectively in the state\nInstituted standards-based grading and standards-based report cards to increase\neducational communication with parents\nImplemented fully inclusive Special Education programs as well as new levels of service\nto meet the needs of our students\n\u2018Implemented and aligned new standards, curricula, materials, and assessments that\nincreased student achievement\nUpgraded district technology infrastructure and improved the computer accessibility\nCreated District strategic plan, Vision 2020, with stakeholder collaboration\nStandardized personnel practices that adhere to legal standards and regulations\nInstituted financial efficiencies that allow for greater resource flexibility\n\nAcademic Record\n\nBachelor of Arts, History Education, December 2001,\n\u2018The College of New Jersey\n\nMasters of Educati\n\n\u2018School Leadership, May 2005,\n\nWilmington University\n\nDoctorate Coursework, Educational Leadership\n\nUniversity of Delaware\nAdministrative Experience _\n\u2018Administrator (Curriculum and Instruction) Lady Liberty Academy\n8/2016-Present \u2018Newark, NI\nChief Executive Officer Striving for Blite Education\n972014-8/2016 Middletown, DE\nSuperintendent Highland Park Public Schools\n8/2013-9/2014 Highland Park, NJ\nExecutive Director of Regional Achievement NJ Department of Education\n\n72012-82013 (accepted position as Superintendent) \u2018Trenton, NJ",
